
# IMPORTANT COMMANDS TO MEMORISE

## Git Command Cheat Sheet

- Check Git version:

    git --version

- Start repository:

    git init

- Check status:

    git status

- See changes:

    git diff

- Stage file:

    git add filename

- Stage everything:

    git add .

- Commit:

    git commit -m "message"

- View history:

    git log

- Short history:

    git log --oneline

- Create branch:

    git branch branch-name

- Create and switch branch:

    git switch -c branch-name

- Switch branch:

    git switch branch-name

- List branches:

    git branch

- Merge branch:

    git merge branch-name

- Download remote changes:

    git fetch

- Download and integrate changes:

    git pull

- Upload commits:

    git push

- Clone repository:

    git clone <url>

- Add remote:

    git remote add origin <url>

- View remotes:

    git remote -v

- Temporarily save changes:

    git stash

- Restore stashed changes:

    git stash pop

- Undo a commit safely:

    git revert <commit>

- Restore a file:

    git restore filename

